+The reviewers’ extension to the p. 202 row is wrong. There the functional outcome being scored is that intended head movement changes the rendered field; external tracking achieved that outcome through a different mechanism. `RIGHT ANSWER, WRONG REASON` is exactly the permitted verdict for an outcome match with a mechanism miss, provided the row names that outcome precisely.
+
+**Fix:** Split teletaxy into an object row (`OPEN` unless a dated nerve-linked path is receipted) and a problem row (light-speed delay bounds teleoperation → `HIT`). Keep the head-tracking row, but word the Lem cell as the functional outcome.
